    "title": "San Antonio Spurs at LA Clippers: Odds, Injury Updates, How to Watch and More",
    "text": "Date: March 16, 2026Time: 10 p.m. ETVenue: Intuit DomeTV: PeacockStreaming: Check local listingsRadio: AM 570 LA Sports, 1200 WOAIBuy tickets: Buy Spurs at Clippers tickets on StubHubThe Spurs have enjoyed a six-game homestand but will soon have to dust off their road jerseys. They will head out to take on the LA Clippers at 10:00 p.m. on Monday at Intuit Dome. The two teams have allowed few points on average (the Spurs 111.8, the Clippers 112.6) so any points scored will be well earned.AdvertisementOn Saturday, the Spurs were able to grind out a solid win over the Hornets, taking the game 115-102.Victor Wembanyama had another great game (as he tends to do), dropping a double-double with 32 points and 12 rebounds. The game also marked Wembanyama's 18th in a row with at least one block.Meanwhile, the Clippers came into the game on Saturday with a huge advantage in the spread, but given the result that advantage might've gone to their heads. They fell 118-109 to the Kings. LA's loss signaled the end of their four-game winning streak.AdvertisementThe loss doesn't tell the whole story though, as several players had good games. One of the most active was Darius Garland, who posted 25 points and 7 assists. The team also got some help from Kawhi Leonard, who went 13-for-23 en route to 31 points and 6 rebounds.San Antonio has been performing incredibly well recently as they've won 17 of their last 19 contests. That's provided a nice bump to their 49-18 record this season. The victories were due in large part to their offensive performance across that stretch, as they averaged 123.5 points over those games. As for LA, their defeat dropped their record down to 34-33.San Antonio Spurs at LA Clippers Odds, Line and SpreadBetting lines as of 03/16/2026 at 11:41 AM ET. Odds subject to change.AdvertisementMoneyline (ML): Spurs -402 | Clippers +313Against the spread (ATS): Spurs -9.5 (-110) | Clippers +9.5 (-110)Over/Under (O/U): 230.5 (O: -110 | U: -110)San Antonio Spurs Injury ReportDavid Jones Garcia (Ankle) - Out for the SeasonLuke Kornet (Knee) - outLA Clippers Injury ReportYanic Konan Niederhäuser (Foot) - Out for the SeasonKawhi Leonard (Ankle) - day-to-dayBradley Beal (Hip) - Out for the SeasonSpurs vs. Clippers: Schedule ImpactSpurs: Playing on normal rest (1 day off). Record in this situation this season: 28-8SAS: won 13 of last 14 games with regular restClippers: Playing on normal rest (1 day off). Record in this situation this season: 23-15LAC: three straight wins with regular restSpurs vs. Clippers: Head-to-Head in 2025-26 SeasonSpurs vs. Clippers: AnalysisWhy the Spurs Can Win: SAS: 6-2 ATS in last 8 games on the roadWhy the Clippers Can Win: LAC: 7-1 ATS in last 8 games as the underdogDisclosure: Some or all of this content may have been generated by AI. While we strive for accuracy, AI can occasionally produce incorrect information. If you buy something via one of our links, we may earn a commission.AdvertisementThis story was originally published by Athlon Sports on Mar 16, 2026, where it first appeared in the NBA section. Add Athlon Sports as a Preferred Source by clicking here.",
